{"authored" [{"question" "q-37131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=xy+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z$ that passes through the point $P(0,1,1).$\n\nGive the full level set, including the necessary range restriction from the principal real arcsine.\n\nHint: Compute $f(0,1,1)$, then use the principal range $-\\pi/2\\le\\arcsin z\\le\\pi/2$ before taking sine." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-37131/review.json" "file_sha256" "ae3d910d204576c9bc129a41084637d08ed54c0731ce1716b1cb519ebcaec88d" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-37131/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "21f2cd6f2982b03e0895b7d892437b3294196d97586ce042498ece5cd30ff187" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-37131/verification.json" "basis" 2290 "rationale" "Keep original f and point. Principal arcsine gives the exact level set z=cos(xy),0≤xy≤π. The unrestricted source relation includes extra points. Append a complete choice in a new field version, preserving original source a and historical component identities."} {"question" "q-37131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The level surface through $P=(0,1,1)$ has level constant\n$$c=f(0,1,1)=0+\\arcsin(1)=\\frac{\\pi}{2}.$$\nThus $xy+\\arcsin z=\\pi/2$, or $\\arcsin z=\\pi/2-xy$. The principal real arcsine takes values in $[-\\pi/2,\\pi/2]$. Therefore\n$$-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le\\frac{\\pi}{2}-xy\\le\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad 0\\le xy\\le\\pi.$$\nTaking sine gives $z=\\sin(\\pi/2-xy)=\\cos(xy)$. Conversely, if $0\\le xy\\le\\pi$ and $z=\\cos(xy)$, then $\\pi/2-xy$ lies in the principal arcsine range, so $\\arcsin z=\\pi/2-xy$ and $f(x,y,z)=\\pi/2$. The exact full level set is\n$$\\boxed{\\{(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3:z=\\cos(xy),\\ 0\\le xy\\le\\pi\\}}.$$\nThe range restriction is essential. For instance $(x,y,z)=(2\\pi,1,1)$ satisfies $z=\\cos(xy)$, but $f(2\\pi,1,1)=2\\pi+\\pi/2=5\\pi/2$, not $\\pi/2$. The source's revealed answer a provides the algebraic relation but omits the restriction. Its original prompt, options, source grade and solution remain preserved; the study choice supplies the complete level set without changing the original function or point." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-37131/review.json" "file_sha256" "ae3d910d204576c9bc129a41084637d08ed54c0731ce1716b1cb519ebcaec88d" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-37131/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "21f2cd6f2982b03e0895b7d892437b3294196d97586ce042498ece5cd30ff187" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-37131/verification.json" "basis" 2290 "rationale" "Keep original f and point. Principal arcsine gives the exact level set z=cos(xy),0≤xy≤π. The unrestricted source relation includes extra points. Append a complete choice in a new field version, preserving original source a and historical component identities."} {"question" "q-37131" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=\\cos(xy),\\quad 0\\le xy\\le\\pi"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-37131/review.json" "file_sha256" "ae3d910d204576c9bc129a41084637d08ed54c0731ce1716b1cb519ebcaec88d" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-37131/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "21f2cd6f2982b03e0895b7d892437b3294196d97586ce042498ece5cd30ff187" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-37131/verification.json" "basis" 2290 "rationale" "Keep original f and point. Principal arcsine gives the exact level set z=cos(xy),0≤xy≤π. The unrestricted source relation includes extra points. Append a complete choice in a new field version, preserving original source a and historical component identities."} {"question" "q-37131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=xy+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z$ that passes through the point $P(0,1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068037/state.json" "file_sha256" "d84c2251596b91cc10e0a031c222de37aff3a7e15241c70f709bc0c7cbfedc21" "basis" 2289 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068037/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,1,1) & =0\\cdot 1+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ xy+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z & =\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-xy \\\\ z & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-xy) \\\\ z & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(0,1,1)$ is the surface $z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068037/state.json" "file_sha256" "d84c2251596b91cc10e0a031c222de37aff3a7e15241c70f709bc0c7cbfedc21" "basis" 2289 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068037/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068037/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25202b02c58253dd349657c72e1ea1dd909de088ce40ffba57ffc6d14b895a6b" "basis" 2289 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068037/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [] "usage" {"q-37131" []} "basis" 2290 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186357002 17592186357003 17592186357004 17592186357005 17592186357006 17592186357022] "immutable_fields" [[17592186357021 :answer-field/correct] [17592186357021 :answer-field/id] [17592186357021 :answer-field/key] [17592186357021 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
